proof='Fix u inV and put q(a)=p+a(u-p),0<=a<=1. Feasibility follows from convexity ofV. Actual minimality and convexity of f give f(p)+h(p)<=f(q(a))+h(q(a))<=(1-a)f(p)+a f(u)+h(q(a)). Hence H(a)=a(f(u)-f(p))+h(q(a))-h(p)>=0=H(0). Differentiate only h along the affine segment: Hprime(0)=f(u)-f(p)+Dh(p)[u-p]. At a minimum on[0,1], the positive tangent direction1 gives Hprime(0)>=0. Rearranging yields f(p)-f(u)<=Dh(p)[u-p]. This proves the loss comparison from an actual minimum, without a supplied regret/stability bound or differentiability of the loss.'
